# fixedbugs, defect 2389, 2026-11-09, the shapes beside the temporary.
#
# SYMPTOM: a group binding a C function named `hero_here`, the place every C
# call's block declares before the call, was *internal error* at exit 2: the
# call read the block's own record, *called object type 'HeroPlace' is not a
# function*. `found`, the entry a map lookup's block declares, is of the same
# kind, the emitter writing it by name.
#
# FIX: every name the emitter declares inside a body is one of
# `emit/shadowed.hero`'s, a bound function of such a name reached through an
# accessor, so both calls print.

extern "fixedbugs-2389-a-bound-c-function-named-as-a-call-s-place-builds.h"
    function hero_here(x: i64) -> i64
    function found(x: i64) -> i64

function main()
    print(hero_here(x: 41))
    ages = {"ziggy": 21}
    print(found(x: ages["ziggy"].must()))
